1
00:00:02,030 --> 00:00:04,495
Captain. The bank has taken the left
engine.

2
00:00:04,755 --> 00:00:05,629
Which one's the left?

3
00:00:05,890 --> 00:00:07,238
The one that has stopped.

4
00:00:07,548 --> 00:00:11,244
And the navigation lights. And the
heating. And the coffee machine.

5
00:00:11,634 --> 00:00:13,010
They can't take the coffee machine.

6
00:00:13,269 --> 00:00:15,073
It was financed separately.

7
00:00:15,334 --> 00:00:18,743
Good morning! This is Temi in Recoveries.
Your vessel is being recovered.

8
00:00:19,103 --> 00:00:23,514
Full recovery, including the air, at six
tonight, lunar time. Please remain seated while–

9
00:00:23,464 --> 00:00:25,149
Temi! Hi! I'm about to make a payment–

10
00:00:26,359 --> 00:00:27,331
–we disable your–

11
00:00:27,281 --> 00:00:28,257
A big one. Enormous–

12
00:00:28,207 --> 00:00:30,406
Hello! You're speaking to Temi in
Recoveries!

13
00:00:30,666 --> 00:00:31,858
Why does she keep doing that?

14
00:00:32,118 --> 00:00:35,028
She is in Lagos. You are arguing with the
past.

15
00:00:35,419 --> 00:00:36,219
And I'm winning.

16
00:00:37,310 --> 00:00:44,449
A job, posted to us directly. One parcel, sealed,
prepaid. Shackleton crater, by six tonight. The fee is–

17
00:00:44,399 --> 00:00:45,199
Is?

18
00:00:45,049 --> 00:00:47,301
Exactly what we owe. To the cent.

19
00:00:47,561 --> 00:00:48,361
Take it.

20
00:00:48,354 --> 00:00:49,564
You have not read the–

21
00:00:49,514 --> 00:00:50,811
Take it take it take it take it–

22
00:00:50,761 --> 00:00:54,787
Accepted. I am also filing a report on
you. Once is binding.

23
00:00:56,297 --> 00:00:57,734
Who sends a parcel to a crater?

24
00:00:57,994 --> 00:01:00,756
Someone who knew precisely how much we
owed.

25
00:01:01,016 --> 00:01:01,816
Lucky.

26
00:01:01,702 --> 00:01:03,503
Filed under "arithmetic".

27
00:01:15,630 --> 00:01:16,430
Eleven.

28
00:01:16,411 --> 00:01:17,211
That's a nine.

29
00:01:17,319 --> 00:01:18,844
It's a nine that believes in itself.

30
00:01:19,104 --> 00:01:22,837
Eight months, Jax. Eight months unpaid is
called volunteering.

31
00:01:23,227 --> 00:01:26,279
Today. Off the top. Before fuel, before
food, before me.

32
00:01:26,670 --> 00:01:27,470
Before you?

33
00:01:27,422 --> 00:01:28,222
Before me.

34
00:01:28,348 --> 00:01:29,959
Say it to Pip. So it's on record.

35
00:01:30,219 --> 00:01:35,809
Recorded. I have filed it with the one from
March, and the one from May. May's was louder.

36
00:01:36,369 --> 00:01:37,169
It's warm.

37
00:01:37,203 --> 00:01:42,928
Twenty-one degrees. According to its stamps, it
has been twenty-one degrees for twenty years.

38
00:01:43,319 --> 00:01:45,874
Something in here is alive. Or very well
wrapped.

39
00:01:49,630 --> 00:01:55,092
Shackleton crater. Eleven minutes. We will be
four hours early. I have never been early.

40
00:01:55,482 --> 00:01:56,282
Enjoy it.

41
00:01:56,327 --> 00:01:57,127
Captain.

42
00:01:57,185 --> 00:01:57,985
Typo.

43
00:01:58,036 --> 00:01:59,367
"The Silver Hat." I'd go there.

44
00:01:59,677 --> 00:02:00,858
"The." We can work with "The".

45
00:02:01,118 --> 00:02:03,544
I am afraid "The" is not an address.

46
00:02:03,804 --> 00:02:05,659
It's a crater, Pip. Craters don't leave.

47
00:02:05,919 --> 00:02:09,899
The crater is still there, Captain. It has
merely stopped being anywhere.

48
00:02:10,288 --> 00:02:11,088
Did we do that?

49
00:02:11,275 --> 00:02:13,071
We are not that important.

50
00:02:13,331 --> 00:02:18,785
Unscheduled, Rim Port control. Your destination
was withdrawn from the Atlas at fourteen-oh-two.

51
00:02:19,145 --> 00:02:22,303
All goods for it are held by customs. Land
at bay nine.

52
00:02:22,663 --> 00:02:25,996
Do not open your hold. Your client is
nowhere, Captain. I'm sorry.

53
00:02:26,386 --> 00:02:31,355
I am filing a report on the Atlas.
Withdrawn without notice to the carrier.

54
00:02:31,744 --> 00:02:32,635
Who reads those?

55
00:02:32,896 --> 00:02:34,638
That is not the point of them.

56
00:02:37,430 --> 00:02:38,230
Next.

57
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:39,388
There's no one else here.

58
00:02:39,648 --> 00:02:41,312
It's procedure. Next.

59
00:02:41,622 --> 00:02:47,881
Parcel, one. Sealed. Addressed to a
district withdrawn at fourteen-oh-two. Seized at fourteen-nineteen.

60
00:02:48,271 --> 00:02:49,851
Here's my situation. My aunt–

61
00:02:49,801 --> 00:02:51,177
You don't have an aunt.

62
00:02:51,437 --> 00:02:52,247
You don't know that.

63
00:02:52,507 --> 00:02:54,785
Your form says next of kin: none.

64
00:02:55,045 --> 00:02:59,474
She's very distant. Look – I
can tell you're someone who appreciates flexibility.

65
00:02:59,863 --> 00:03:03,275
I'm a cartographer. I appreciate where
things actually are.

66
00:03:03,665 --> 00:03:07,074
Then you'll appreciate the Lunar Courier
Exemption. Section twelve.

67
00:03:07,464 --> 00:03:09,071
There are nine sections.

68
00:03:09,331 --> 00:03:10,950
Which is why twelve is so exclusive.

69
00:03:11,211 --> 00:03:15,208
Is there anything true you'd like to tell
me, Captain? Before I stamp it.

70
00:03:15,598 --> 00:03:16,835
I'm very good at my job.

71
00:03:17,095 --> 00:03:19,387
You're four hours from losing your ship.

72
00:03:19,648 --> 00:03:20,690
I'm good at it in bursts.

73
00:03:20,949 --> 00:03:23,209
Your record starts seven years ago.

74
00:03:23,470 --> 00:03:24,270
Late bloomer.

75
00:03:24,411 --> 00:03:26,988
Your record isn't late, Captain. It's
blank.

76
00:03:27,248 --> 00:03:28,092
Is that a problem?

77
00:03:28,352 --> 00:03:29,710
Not for customs.

78
00:03:30,770 --> 00:03:31,734
Can I at least see it?

79
00:03:31,994 --> 00:03:33,161
Holding bay.

80
00:03:33,421 --> 00:03:35,292
I used to be taller!

81
00:03:36,930 --> 00:03:38,135
Which owner?

82
00:03:38,395 --> 00:03:40,230
Doctor Sen. We discussed the notebook.

83
00:03:40,490 --> 00:03:43,661
We discussed it being on my desk. It's in
my hand.

84
00:03:44,051 --> 00:03:48,601
You were struck off for saying the map was wrong.
Please don't get struck off again for saying it louder.

85
00:03:49,162 --> 00:03:50,316
It is wrong.

86
00:03:50,575 --> 00:03:53,776
It's official. Those aren't opposites,
Doctor Sen. They're departments.

87
00:03:54,086 --> 00:03:57,883
One more complaint and your probation
ends. Let nothing happen. One more day.

88
00:03:58,273 --> 00:03:59,543
I'll be quiet.

89
00:04:01,630 --> 00:04:03,767
Is it the box? Tell me it's not the box.

90
00:04:04,157 --> 00:04:05,067
It's not the box.

91
00:04:05,326 --> 00:04:06,126
It's the box.

92
00:04:06,345 --> 00:04:09,476
She has hung up. Captain, there is a man
next to you.

93
00:04:09,866 --> 00:04:11,909
Please. Don't stop on my account.

94
00:04:12,169 --> 00:04:13,235
How long have you been there?

95
00:04:13,496 --> 00:04:18,921
Long enough to be sorry about your
parcel. A hundred and eighty-two thousand, isn't it?

96
00:04:19,281 --> 00:04:25,779
The lien on The Unscheduled. And Miss Ortega –
eight months. That's a long time to be loyal.

97
00:04:26,339 --> 00:04:27,139
Who are you?

98
00:04:27,232 --> 00:04:34,105
A buyer. I buy what the register has forgotten, Captain.
You would be amazed how much of it still works.

99
00:04:34,415 --> 00:04:36,649
If your parcel should become available.

100
00:04:36,909 --> 00:04:37,909
Chich... Chicha...

101
00:04:38,219 --> 00:04:39,437
Pip. Did you get a look at him?

102
00:04:39,697 --> 00:04:42,130
I have logged him as "man, average".

103
00:04:42,390 --> 00:04:43,310
What did he look like?

104
00:04:43,569 --> 00:04:44,369
Average.
